
TOON 3.0

  Open .toon files or use --toon for standard input. TOON is shown using the
  existing JSON Line/Data views. Searches use normalized JSON text.

  yt                  Copy the complete focused value as canonical TOON.
  pt                  Print the complete focused value as canonical TOON.
  :wt file            Write the document as canonical TOON to a new file.
  :writetoon file      Same as :wt.
  :wt! file           Create or replace a file after encoding succeeds.
  :writetoon! file     Same as :wt!.

  TOON output requires unique string keys, finite JSON numbers, and at most
  256 nested containers. Numbers that would lose decimal precision are rejected.
  Whole-document output requires one root; yt and pt can select one subtree.
  Existing JSON write/copy/print commands keep their existing output format.
  Non-terminal output passes selected TOON input through unchanged.

  toon-spec: 3.0. TOON 4.x syntax is not supported.
